Z||000008||FLASHY||02-06-2001||04:46 PM||||Hey guys! As you can tell I'm new here and I just want to say it's great to see the wealth of info evryone has to offer. When I went to Art College I wanted to know if there were any ways to make something look chrome without actually plating it. I was told one way is to make sure the surface is made smooth as possible, then spray it with silver paint (I'm sure most of you probably know, many thin coats is better than one or two thick coats as it gives you a more even and smooth surface), then spray that surface with many caots of high-gloss varnish or lacquer. Apparently the more clear-coats you add the more it will look chrome. Now I say "apparently" because I have not tried this myself but I was told it's quite effective. If you are considering this method I'd try it on a scrap surface first because I'd hate to get a bad reputation right off the bat. Who knows...it may not look exactly like chrome but it still might look great! Anyway I hope that helps somewhat and I'm looking forward to having my questions and concerns answered in the future. <p>[This message has been edited by FLASHY (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000009||TheFiero64||02-06-2001||05:37 PM||||Welcome to the forum FLASHY.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
