Z||000012||bHooper||02-07-2001||02:10 PM||||no one answered my question, so i will ask again....<P>if you used aluminum, chrome, stainless, or any other metal, for console face plates, wouldn't it be too hot to touch in the summer?  or is that just a southern thing?  as it is, my center console/arm rest, gets too hot, if i leave the roof off in the summer.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000013||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||03:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>no one answered my question, so i will ask again....<P>if you used aluminum, chrome, stainless, or any other metal, for console face plates, wouldn't it be too hot to touch in the summer?  or is that just a southern thing?  as it is, my center console/arm rest, gets too hot, if i leave the roof off in the summer.<P>hoop</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You have a good point.. It might be a little warm on a  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> 100deg + day. I ordered the full kit so I will let you know if its worth it or not.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Carl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||12
Z||000014||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||03:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by the need for speed:<BR><B>can anyone see what it says on the glove box?i love the way it looks!haze_performance would love to see some pics when it is all put to gether on your car. Also did you get a price on the glove box <P>[This message has been edited by the need for speed (edited 02-07-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The glovebox says "SUPERCHARGED". The shop said the owner had the steel cover made himself. They dont sell it. The 7pc. kit includes:<P>1. Speedo<P>2. Radio/Heater<P>3. Aux. gauge <P>4. Shifter<P>5. Cig. lighter cover replacement<P>6 & 7. Left & Right heater vent cover<P>I just installed the Polished wheel & Install kit. I just ordered the pedal covers (Chrome) and Im going to order a Holley Chrome 4-point roll bar & Mr. Mikes 500 Black/Light Silver Seats. Im still looking for something to do with the door panels.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||10
Z||000015||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||03:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Plastic is dipped into a special plating to chrome it. Sort of how they do for models. I have no idea who could do it. Maybe Revell/Monogram models in Des Plaines?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I called... They want NOTHING to do with custom work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||9
Z||000016||ray b||02-07-2001||04:03 PM||||[chrome]willnot stick to plastic but alum.<BR>canbe vacume deposited to look like chrome.<BR>thats how plastic models are chromed.canbe done in colors or tints but must be clear coated or will rub off .canbe hard to find co. that will do small order and parts must be very clean and any nicks will show thru.<BR>look in big city phone book under vacume plating.   ray||||reg||1
Z||000017||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||04:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>[chrome]willnot stick to plastic but alum.<BR>canbe vacume deposited to look like chrome.<BR>thats how plastic models are chromed.canbe done in colors or tints but must be clear coated or will rub off .canbe hard to find co. that will do small order and parts must be very clean and any nicks will show thru.<BR>look in big city phone book under vacume plating.   ray</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the info....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||12
